{"id": "EUVD-2026-67553", "enisaUuid": "7fb2782e-44d6-3de7-b7f1-2cc41183d6dc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndriver core: use READ_ONCE() for dev->driver in dev_has_sync_state()\n\ndev_has_sync_state() reads dev->driver twice without holding\ndevice_lock() -- once for the NULL check and once to dereference\n->sync_state. Some callers only hold device_links_write_lock, which\ndoesn't prevent a concurrent unbind from clearing dev->driver via\ndevice_unbind_cleanup().\n\nFix it by reading dev->driver exactly once with READ_ONCE(), pairing\nwith the WRITE_ONCE() in device_set_driver().", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:49:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:26:32", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89789e4c141904506163dcb91c7289a074573931", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51b3e1de53ee5b7775c7ff90e67fdb2665fce938", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/358697929351f619143f59c6a8a15a4994748b79", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e79e0180515b31b2e2244dc3d256fd8b5a07021", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/860885fcd2611bca8c28dac8b2c1c7ff160f763e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc77f0d91e3214e4292208f02a1dc09a31f9aac7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b0f4082a09760939588135d60a8e9cc994bfa3e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9506871a8ea304cde48ff4a57226df2aadddae3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jprm-rcxh-4jgp", "CVE-2026-80677"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1cc77af3-0212-3ee0-96e6-77de9369bc39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ac338acf514e7b578fa9e3742ec2c292323b4c1a <89789e4c141904506163dcb91c7289a074573931"}, {"id": "22bbf6aa-1761-311d-869d-aba6102e4008", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ac338acf514e7b578fa9e3742ec2c292323b4c1a <358697929351f619143f59c6a8a15a4994748b79"}, {"id":